From 6fc07453c0c8f655e276e0762c7df3c9a5a998c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:26:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BOOTCLEAR9050: HT9050 asks once after boot whether to clear
 the machine data restored from machinerecord.dat -- EastSun 1008 'every
 start, if the machine has material, ask whether to clear: Yes clears, No
 carries on'.

cinitial.cpp (end of file): W906_BootAskClearMachine9050. Runs once, on the first DoAllProcess pass after wb_serve installed the
  YES / NO web hook (the boot sequence cannot ask). HT9050 only, idle only. "Has material" = SaveMachineRecord's own list (manual
  trays, Tray Y, plates, Auto1-6 and cars) or HasICUnderMachine(). Yes = golden InitialMachine + Loader / Empty stack counts -1
  (re-probe) + Auto1-3 counts 0 + SaveMachineRecord; No = keep; answer 3 (another box open) = ask again next pass. RecordProcess logs it.
csystem.cpp DoAllProcess: the call, same line as FLOWTRACE / TRAYZTHICK.
Why: after a restart golden restores Tray Y 'has tray' while iLoaderLayerCount_9050 starts at -1, so DoLoad_9050 case 1 parks
  Loader Z at Down[-1] = 22300 instead of probing (10:14 oplog).
tests: test_flow9050_tray.cpp [BC] (7 checks), Flow9050_Tray 137/137; W6_6_CSystemCycle, FP9050_Pure / Index, HT9050_ProdFlow /
  DryRun passed. Debug and release linked.
Not in this commit: EastSun's own acatchtray.cpp / asendic_Loader.cpp probe edits (09:48 / 09:56), left in his tree.
Backups D:\HT9045\_review\*.bak_bootclear9050_20261008_102348. WORKLOG row 201.

